{"id":"gotcha-example-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Example: Truthy check on numeric values fails for explicit zero - if (value) is false when value === 0.","recommendation":"Use !== undefined or !== null instead of truthy checks when the value could legitimately be 0 or empty string.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"coderabbit","reference":"PR review","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["javascript","type-coercion","validation"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-mcp-asyncio-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"Using asyncio.run() inside a FastAPI async route raises RuntimeError ('This event loop is already running') because FastAPI already runs an event loop. MCP's stdio_client is async-only, so it cannot be called directly from a FastAPI route.","recommendation":"Wrap any asyncio.run() / MCP call in a ThreadPoolExecutor worker: `with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as ex: ex.submit(lambda: asyncio.run(...)).result(timeout=30)`. The worker thread has no running loop so asyncio.run() succeeds.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"feature/003-inline-pr-comments implementation","date":"2026-06-16"}],"tags":["mcp","asyncio","fastapi","threading","python"],"affectedFiles":["backend/mcp/client.py","backend/mcp/**/*.py"],"affectedServices":["GitHubMCPClient"],"createdAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-mcp-starlette-version-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"pip install mcp silently upgrades starlette to >=1.3.x, which is incompatible with FastAPI <=0.121.x (FastAPI requires starlette<0.50.0). The app will fail to start with ImportError or attribute errors after the install.","recommendation":"After installing mcp, immediately re-pin starlette: `pip install \"starlette<0.50.0\"`. Add this constraint to requirements.txt so it survives future installs.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"feature/003-inline-pr-comments — pip install mcp broke FastAPI startup","date":"2026-06-16"}],"tags":["mcp","starlette","fastapi","dependencies","pip","python"],"affectedFiles":["requirements.txt","requirements*.txt"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-fastapi-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"FastAPI APIRouter does not support exception_handler(). Calling @router.exception_handler(ValueError) raises AttributeError: 'APIRouter' object has no attribute 'exception_handler'.","recommendation":"Register exception handlers on the FastAPI app instance in main.py using @app.exception_handler(ExcType), never on an APIRouter.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"feature/004-provider-selection session","date":"2026-06-17"}],"tags":["fastapi","exception-handling","python"],"affectedFiles":["backend/main.py","backend/routers/**/*.py"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-git-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"git checkout -b feature/xxx develop fails or inherits dirty working-tree state when there are uncommitted changes including untracked files.","recommendation":"When working tree is dirty: (1) git stash -u, (2) git branch -f <branch> <base>, (3) git checkout <branch>, (4) git stash pop. This force-resets the branch pointer without touching uncommitted work.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"feature/004-provider-selection session","date":"2026-06-17"}],"tags":["git","branching","workflow"],"affectedFiles":[],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"gotcha-ruff-001","type":"gotcha","fact":"ruff F401 fires on imports in test files that are referenced only in comments or only used as type hints but not in runtime assertions.","recommendation":"Keep test imports lean: only import what appears in actual assert/call expressions. Remove imports only referenced in docstrings or inline comments.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"human","reference":"feature/004-provider-selection session","date":"2026-06-17"}],"tags":["ruff","linting","python","testing"],"affectedFiles":["backend/tests/**/*.py"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-06-17T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
